# Method

Makes about 10-12 goląbki (one per cabbage leaf).

1. **Prep the cabbage.** Core the cabbage (cut a cone around the stem with a paring knife, ~5cm deep, twist out). Place core-side down in a large pot of simmering water. As outer leaves soften, peel them off and lay on a tea towel. Trim the thick rib at the base of each leaf. Keep the dark outer leaves for lining the pot.
2. **Cook the rice halfway.** Cook for about half the time on the packet — semi-cooked only, it finishes inside the rolls. Cool.
3. **Sauté the onion.** Finely chop the onion and sauté in the butter until translucent. Cool slightly.
4. **Make the filling.** Combine pork mince, cooled rice, sautéed onion, crushed garlic, chopped parsley, marjoram, paprika, salt and black pepper. Mix well with your hands.
5. **Roll.** A generous spoonful of filling on each leaf, fold the sides in, roll up firmly like a burrito. One parcel per leaf. Place seam-side down.
6. **Line the pot.** Line a heavy pot or Dutch oven with the reserved dark outer cabbage leaves to stop the rolls catching and to keep steam in.
7. **Pack and cook.** Pack the rolls in seam-side down, snugly in layers. Dissolve the stock cube in ~2 cups boiling water, then pour over with the tin of chopped tomatoes and all the passata. Liquid should nearly cover the rolls. Bring to a gentle simmer on the stove, cover, then either simmer 45-50 min or transfer to a 180°C oven for 60 min.
8. **Finish the sauce.** Lift the rolls out carefully with a slotted spoon onto a warm plate; cover loosely with foil. Put the pot back on medium-high heat, uncovered, and let the cooking liquid bubble and reduce for 5-10 minutes until glossy and spoonable, stirring occasionally so the bottom doesn't catch. Taste and adjust seasoning.
9. **Serve.** Plate over mashed potatoes with the sauce spooned over.
